% Architecture detail

Plans one vocal-over-instrumental layer from read-only analysis. find_siblings finds analyzed full mixes of the same song (same core title, overlapping artist, explicit before clean). align_to_sibling cross-correlates voice-band (300-3400 Hz) onset envelopes at ~10 ms frames and refines the peak; it is usable only when the peak beats the best rival (>0.5 s away) by MIN_ALIGN_CONFIDENCE and the two halves of the acapella give one offset within 20 ms (same tempo, no edit). The sibling's measured snare phase (brain.onset_analysis.measure_backbeat_timing, source seconds) minus the offset becomes the vocal's snare phase and the sibling's BPM its tempo. The instrumental's snare phase is measured directly. Snares on 2 and 4 are therefore exact on both sides; count 1 vs 3 stays `guessed` (the count-1 detector agreed with Ernest only 9 of 14 times) and the A/B alternative is a whole snare cycle (+/-2 beats); a 1-beat shift is refused because it puts the snare on 1 and 3. plan_layer(vocal_id, bed_id, ...) keeps the vocal at its own speed and moves the instrumental to the vocal's tempo (keylock on), refuses tempos more than 8% apart, starts the bed at its cue, enters the vocal's count-1 candidate (first kick beat at or after first word minus one beat, inside the chosen vocal_from/vocal_to section) on a bed kick beat lead_bars whole bars after the bed's first kick, starts the vocal deck one bar early in its silence but never before the chosen section, lasts to the last sustained word, then a 16-beat bed fade. Levels: with ReplayGain on both tracks in Mixxx (enabled in Ernest's mixxx.cfg) trust it; otherwise equalize gated loudness by turning the louder one down; the bed sits about 2 dB under the voice; a full-mix bed dips mids to 0.35 and highs to 0.7, an instrumental bed mids to 0.8. With no usable full mix the backbeat is `unverified` and a warning says so. Measurements cache in brain/data/stem_layers.json keyed by path, size and mtime. describe(plan) prints the plan in plain